Restore a writable umask around the bundled-gem loop.

rbinstall.rb sets File.umask(0222) globally, and Gem::Installer creates each
gem directory with FileUtils.mkdir_p and no explicit mode, so the directory
lands at 0555 and the first file written into it fails with EACCES. Upstream
compensates only after the loop has finished -- the "fix directory permissions"
chmod below -- which is too late.

Releases that also ship the gems unpacked take RbInstall::UnpackedInstaller
instead, which chmods each directory itself, so they never reach this path.

--- a/tool/rbinstall.rb
+++ b/tool/rbinstall.rb
@@ -777,6 +777,7 @@
   if defined?(Zlib)
     Gem.instance_variable_set(:@ruby, with_destdir(File.join(bindir, ruby_install_name)))
     silent = Gem::SilentUI.new
+    gem_umask = File.umask(0022)
     gems.each do |gem|
       inst = Gem::Installer.new(gem, options)
       inst.spec.extension_dir = with_destdir(inst.spec.extension_dir)
@@ -788,6 +789,7 @@
       gemname = File.basename(gem)
       puts "#{" "*30}#{gemname}"
     end
+    File.umask(gem_umask)
     # fix directory permissions
     # TODO: Gem.install should accept :dir_mode option or something
     File.chmod($dir_mode, *Dir.glob(install_dir+"/**/"))
